            <ArticleTitle>[Cardiomyopathy of the right ventricle revealed by pulmonary embolism].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>963-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of cardiomyopathy of the right ventricle revealed suddenly in a presentation of pulmonary embolism in relation to a large thrombus that developed in an enormous, extremely hypokinetic right ventricle. The scenario suggests dysplasia without rhythm disorder. This case allows a discussion on the multiple variants of arhythmogenic dysplasia of the right ventricle.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
